review_comments:
It's not mandatory to switch from Semaphore  to ManualResetEvent. But in my mind Semaphore is for controlling access to a shared resource, while here we use it to signal that an item has been added to the queue (looks like an event job).

Also it simplifies code a little:
```cs
try
{
    operationSemaphore.Release();
}
catch (Exception)
{
    // Prevent semaphore handles exceeding
}
```
To:
```cs
operationEvent.Set();
```
